---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import Accordion from '../../components/picks-docs/Accordion.astro';
import { PLAN_TABLE, SUPPORT_EMAIL } from '@studpilot/shared';
import { STUDIO_PLUGIN_INSTALL_HREF, STUDIO_PLUGIN_STORE_LIVE } from '../../lib/studio-plugin';

const free = PLAN_TABLE.free;

const general = [
  {
    q: 'Where do I get the StudPilot plugin?',
    a: STUDIO_PLUGIN_STORE_LIVE
      ? `<p>From the Roblox Creator Store, and only from there. The plugin is called <strong>StudPilot Studio</strong> and it is free: <a href="/docs/plugin">The Studio plugin</a> says how to get it and install it.</p>`
      // The closed-store answer takes its link from the shared href. That derivation also keeps it out of the docs search index
      // (src/data/docs-index.ts skips templates), so a search made while the store is open cannot surface the sentence that says it is shut.
      : `<p>Public Studio installation is unavailable right now, so new customers cannot get it yet. You can sign up and use the chat in the meantime. <a href="${STUDIO_PLUGIN_INSTALL_HREF}">Plugin availability</a> says what that means.</p>`,
  },
  {
    q: 'Is StudPilot free?',
    a: `<p>Yes, while it is in beta. The Free plan gives you ${free.creditsPerDay} Credits a day, up to ${free.creditsPerMonth} a month, with no card. Paid plans start later. See <a href="/pricing">Pricing</a> and <a href="/docs/credits-and-limits">Credits &amp; limits</a>.</p>`,
  },
  {
    q: 'Do I need to know how to script?',
    a: `<p>No. StudPilot writes the Luau for you, and you can ask it to explain anything it wrote in plain words.</p>`,
  },
  {
    q: 'How old do I need to be?',
    a: `<p>StudPilot is for people aged 13 and older.</p>`,
  },
  {
    q: 'Can StudPilot publish my game?',
    a: `<p>No. The plugin says it cannot publish. StudPilot builds inside the place you have open, and publishing to Roblox stays something you do yourself, in Studio, with your own account.</p>`,
  },
  {
    // This comment used to say a refund "was not true and could not become true". It became true on 2026-09-20: QuotaDO gained /refund and
    // SessionDO calls it. The answer below still does not promise one, and that is correct rather than stale: closing Studio mid-build pauses
    // the run, which is not a failure that left you nothing, so it is not the case the refund covers. Work that never ran is still never
    // charged, which remains the reason this answer holds.
    q: 'What happens if I close Studio mid-build?',
    a: `<p>The agent notices it lost its hands and pauses the run with a clear message. Work that never ran is never charged: Credits settle against the compute a call actually reported, and a call that did not happen reports nothing. Reopen the place, pair again with a new code, and ask StudPilot to continue. The plan and history are still in the project.</p>`,
  },
  {
    q: 'StudPilot made a change I hate. Now what?',
    // "EACH STUDPILOT BATCH IS ONE NATIVE UNDO STEP" WAS THE WRONG UNIT, and it made Ctrl+Z sound like the whole-run exit. The plugin opens one
    // ChangeHistoryService recording per OPERATION (apps/studpilot-plugin/src/Commands.luau) and the bridge executes a server batch one operation at a
    // time (apps/studpilot-plugin/src/Bridge.luau), so a batch of six writes is six undo steps. The checkpoint is the single-action exit; Ctrl+Z is the
    // fine-grained one.
    a: `<p>Three exits, in order of size: press <kbd>Ctrl+Z</kbd> in Studio to take back the last change (one undo step per change StudPilot made, so a multi-step run needs one press per step); restore the checkpoint taken before the run, which undoes the whole run in one action; or just tell StudPilot what you hate. It can usually fix a wrong turn faster than a rollback.</p>`,
  },
  {
    //[[ THIS ANSWER SAID "Not yet", AND THE FEATURE WAS ALREADY IN THE READER'S OWN ACCOUNT.
    //
    //   The HTTP API shipped the day after this answer was last edited, and nobody came back to it. `GET /v1` answers 401 with "Provide an API key
    //   as `Authorization: Bearer gk_live_…`" on the live worker (a gated surface, not an absent one), and Settings → Connections → API keys
    //   mints, lists, rotates and revokes keys behind nothing but a signed-in session: no plan gate, no allowlist. So the docs denied a capability
    //   the product was handing out, and the reader either never found it or found it and stopped believing the manual.
    //
    //   NO LINK TO A DOCS PAGE, BECAUSE THERE IS NO DOCS PAGE. The API describes itself at GET /v1 and GET /v1/openapi.json, both of which need only a
    //   valid key, and that is what this points at. Inventing an /docs/api href here would trade one false sentence for a dead link.
    //
    //   AND NO SDK. The panel in the app names one; `packages/sdk` is `"private": true` and is published nowhere, so a customer cannot install what
    //   that word promises. Naming it here would spread the same defect onto a second surface.
    q: 'Is there an API or a way to script StudPilot itself?',
    a: `<p>Yes. There is an HTTP API at <code>/v1</code> on the same host as the app, with scoped keys: chat completions, your projects and their transcripts, starting an agent run, a server-sent event stream of run state, and a Model Context Protocol endpoint for MCP clients.</p>
      <p>Mint a key under <strong>Settings &rarr; Connections &rarr; API keys</strong> in the app. You see the secret once, and you can rotate or revoke it from the same panel. The surface documents itself: <code>GET /v1</code> lists every route and the scope it needs, and <code>GET /v1/openapi.json</code> is the machine-readable description. Both accept any valid key. There is no separate docs page for it yet, and no published client library.</p>`,
  },
  {
    q: 'Is there a community, and how do I report a bug?',
    a: `<p>There is a <a href="/discord">StudPilot Discord server</a>. To report a bug or ask for a feature, email <a href="mailto:${SUPPORT_EMAIL}">${SUPPORT_EMAIL}</a> with the project name and roughly when it happened. Screenshots help.</p>`,
  },
];
---

<DocsLayout
  title="FAQ | StudPilot"
  description="Quick answers about the plugin, the free beta, scripting, publishing, interrupted builds, undo and rollback, the API and reporting bugs."
  heading="Frequently asked questions"
  order={6}
  summary="Quick answers to the questions that come up most."
>
  <p>
    Answers to the questions that reach our inbox most. Pricing and quota questions live on the
    <a href="/pricing">pricing page</a>; data questions on
    <a href="/docs/privacy-and-data">privacy &amp; data</a>.
  </p>

  <div class="faq-block">
    <Accordion items={general} />
  </div>
</DocsLayout>

<style>
  .faq-block {
    margin-top: 2rem;
  }
</style>
